{"id": "EUVD-2026-97448", "enisaUuid": "f18bf057-45a9-3c49-a5e2-5e8a19cb59ab", "description": "LogicalDOC Community Edition through 9.3 contains a sql injection vulnerability that allows authenticated users to execute crafted SQL via the firstLetter parameter of TagsDataServlet. Low-privileged attackers can inject UNION SELECT statements returned in the XML tag list to read usernames, email addresses and password hashes from ld_user.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T13:39:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T16:57:49", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/discussions/119", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/commit/8428bfb93f89ab5773019299d17d643c075c4aee", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/blob/9.3/logicaldoc-core/src/main/java/com/logicaldoc/core/document/HibernateDocumentDAO.java#L691", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community/blob/9.3/logicaldoc-webapp/src/main/java/com/logicaldoc/web/data/TagsDataServlet.java#L41", "https://github.com/logicaldoc/community", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/logicaldoc-community-edition-through-9.3-sql-injection-via-tags-xml-firstletter"], "aliases": ["GHSA-cfx3-f25c-pr5c", "CVE-2026-109169"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f1fa4fc-30b2-3728-8d88-391105b2e525", "product": {"name": "LogicalDOC Community Edition", "vendor": {"name": "LogicalDOC"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fd2c307b-520e-3902-9e71-85cc9525581c", "vendor": {"name": "LogicalDOC"}}], "isExploited": false}